From: At30c <PabloAtsoc9993@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m21s: prepare tzdev before starting TEEgris

The F415F vendor declares /dev/tzdev as system:system 0666 and labels it as
tz_user_device, but normal-boot captures showed tzdaemon receiving EACCES.
Apply the intended label and permissions immediately before starting the
daemon instead of relying solely on the legacy ueventd rule.

Keystore2 is part of early_hal and may attempt to initialize before the legacy
TEE daemon publishes vendor.tzdaemon=Ready.  Start it again when TEEgris is
ready so vold can obtain android.system.keystore2.IKeystoreService/default and
finish the file-encryption handoff.

--- a/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
+++ b/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
@@ -3,12 +3,16 @@ on post-fs
     mkdir /mnt/vendor/efs/tee 0700 system system
     mkdir /dev/socket/iwt 0770 system system
     mkdir /dev/socket/iwt/ca 0770 system system
+    restorecon /dev/tzdev
+    chown system system /dev/tzdev
+    chmod 0666 /dev/tzdev
     start tz_service
     start tz_msg_recv
 
 on property:vendor.tzdaemon=Ready
     setprop vendor.TEEGRIS.loaded true
     write /proc/iccc_ready 1
     start tzts_service
+    start keystore2
 
 on property:vendor.tzts_daemon=Ready
 
